# One site, SITE_ADDRESS, proxied to the app. PocketBase is not routed through Caddy.
# On the VPS SITE_ADDRESS is `https://` (Phase 5 spec, Caddy configuration): one catch-all with on-demand TLS for ofl.ink,
# Phase 2's v2 host, every Spare Domain and every Custom Domain. Before Caddy obtains a certificate for a hostname it asks the
# app's TLS Ask over the Compose network, which says yes only to a hostname the app admits (app/server.js, /internal/tls-ask).
# reverse_proxy passes the original Host header on, Caddy's default. In tests SITE_ADDRESS is `:80`: plain HTTP for any Host.
# ASSUMPTION: the ask and `tls { on_demand }` are always present rather than in an env-selected snippet like the PROXY
# protocol's below (rung 1: on the local caddy:2-alpine v2.11.4, `caddy adapt` with SITE_ADDRESS=:80 drops the site's
# `tls { on_demand }` and gives the same :80 server as without both, with no TLS policy, so nothing asks and no certificate is
# obtained; tests/caddy-ask.sh checks both adaptations). Overturned if a Caddy release attaches TLS to a plain-HTTP address;
# the two lines then move into an env-selected snippet.

# PROXY protocol (ticket 45): compose.yaml turns the Operator's PROXY_PROTOCOL_FROM into `off` (empty, as in tests) or
# `on <CIDRs>`, which picks one of these snippets. On, every listener reads a PROXY protocol header from those addresses only,
# ahead of TLS, and takes its source as the client address, so the X-Forwarded-For entry Caddy writes is the Visitor's
# (app/src/click-guard.js). A header from any other address is read and dropped, never trusted. Off, there is no wrapper.
# ASSUMPTION: an env-selected snippet rather than an always-present wrapper with an empty `allow` (rung 1: on the local
# caddy:2-alpine v2.11.4 an empty `allow` still adapts to a proxy_protocol wrapper, which reads and drops a header from any
# address, so Caddy would not behave exactly as without it). Overturned if Caddy gains a Caddyfile conditional.
(proxy_protocol_off) {
}

(proxy_protocol_on) {
	servers {
		listener_wrappers {
			proxy_protocol {
				allow {args[:]}
			}
			tls
		}
	}
}

{
	import proxy_protocol_{$PROXY_PROTOCOL_FROM:off}
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://app:3000/internal/tls-ask
	}
}

{$SITE_ADDRESS} {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	reverse_proxy app:3000
}
